content.text:
The Anthropic Engineering source works again. Run against the live page, it now returns all 24 engineering posts, newest first, starting with "Redesigning source control at Anthropic" (2026-10-13). The tests pass (5 of 5), and the new `/research/` links load. I haven't committed anything.

**What changed:** in [scripts/feeds.mjs](scripts/feeds.mjs), the scraper no longer searches the page for the old `engineeringArticle` text. It now:
- decodes the page's embedded Next.js data and reads the `posts` array as real JSON, so it doesn't depend on the order fields appear in;
- keeps only posts tagged with the engineering team, so related research and news articles elsewhere on the page are left out;
- builds links as `https://www.anthropic.com/research/<slug>`, or uses a post's own `linkedUrl` when it has one;
- trims stray spaces from titles (the newest one starts with a space) and drops posts that are duplicates or have no date.

The parsing is now a separate exported function, `parseAnthropicEngineering`, the same way the Software Lead Weekly scraper is set up, so it can be tested without fetching anything.

**Tests:** I added a small hand-made page, [test/fixtures/anthropic-engineering.html](test/fixtures/anthropic-engineering.html), and two tests in [test/feeds.test.mjs](test/feeds.test.mjs). They cover:
- the `posts` list split across two chunks of the page's data;
- a related article nested inside a post;
- a post from another team;
- a post with its own `linkedUrl`;
- a duplicate and an undated post;
- a page with no `posts` list at all.

The newest post is 16 days old, and the build only shows the last 14 days, so the page won't show any Anthropic posts until they publish a new one. The scraper is working; there's just nothing recent enough yet.
